    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a heavy emphasis on the plus-matchup against Gibson, whose 5.27 xERA makes him the primary target for our core hitters. **Gunnar Henderson** leads the charge with a 76.03 rating; despite a minor penalty for facing an elite hold-out pitcher, his dynamic platoon advantage and second-slot placement make him our most potent offensive engine. Similarly, **Josh Lowe** (70.07) and **Nolan Schanuel** (69.69) benefit significantly from the Gibson matchup. While **Josh Lowe** is buried in the eight-hole, his elite speed profile\u2014critical for our SB-focused strategy\u2014and the favorable SP context keep him locked as an essential start over higher-ordered, lower-upside alternatives. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (71.09) also serves as a pillar today, leveraging a solid BvP track record (42 PA) and a significant platoon edge against Nola to punch well above his base projection.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Jacob Wilson** (56.36) on the bench. He was the final cut, narrowly edged out by **Sam Antonacci** and **Wade Meckler**; while **Jacob Wilson** offers utility, the specific platoon splits and order advantages assigned to **Wade Meckler** in the three-hole against Gibson tipped the scale in his favor for volume purposes. We are also monitoring **Cole Carrigg** (60.27), who faces a stiffer test against Suarez (3.78 xERA) but earns his spot through an elite +14% park factor and the necessary stolen base upside required to maintain our competitive edge in the standings. All starters should be considered green-lit, though users should keep a close watch on **Jackson Merrill** (52.92); his heavy platoon disadvantage against Perez makes him the most volatile element of our current lineup and a candidate for early-inning pinch-hit replacement if the matchup stagnates.",
